  <section id="emdash-bugs"><h2>EmDash Bugs &amp; Friction (For Human Review)</h2><p><a href="/dashboard/emdash-bugs.txt">Versioned reproduction notes, root causes and workarounds</a>. This ledger separates observed sharp edges from confirmed CMS defects; reports to EmDash require human review.</p><ul><li>Standalone Node image transforms needed Sharp declared at the application root.</li><li>Untouched upstream admin/catalog seeding times out locally; cause remains unresolved.</li><li>Concurrent sandbox runners collide on the default workerd port in one network namespace.</li><li>Earlier deployments reached the 10-second stop timeout because runner cleanup left the application HTTP listener open. A merchant launcher now closes HTTP and drains accepted requests before releasing workerd, with eleven offline lifecycle checks and an isolated current-build comparison passing; initial activation was not a live shutdown test. The next normal stop at 22:24 UTC closed admission, drained and deactivated without a forced kill; samples began after restart and establish neither continuous uptime nor background-job drain. Missing encryption configuration is a separate, expected refusal.</li><li>Block Kit Section text collapses newlines; Commerce’s order inspector needs separate wrapping rows. Expected host behavior, not a confirmed CMS defect; repair proposed in Commerce PR #261.</li><li>An automated keyboard reorder of expanded product-detail blocks stopped short; collapsing the blocks first allowed the desired order to save and reload. Cause remains unisolated from timing and scrolling, not a confirmed CMS defect.</li><li>A refused native weight form closes its Shipping disclosure while retaining input. A disposable replay isolates Commerce’s unkeyed-card state transfer; <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/commerce/pull/267">PR #267</a> proposes stable Block Kit identities, without a CMS change. Reopen Shipping to correct in the unchanged signed plugin; this is not an assumed requirement for EmDash to reset local state.</li><li>At phone width, replacing the successfully saved weight form detaches its focused button; the resulting focus-leave event closes Kumo’s Settings sheet. An isolated installed replay reproduces click and keyboard Enter, while desktop retains its controls. Reopen Settings to read the saved value: both phone cases verify 12.5 oz without another save. <a href="/pr-proof/emdash-phone-settings/before-save-390.png">Before save</a> / <a href="/pr-proof/emdash-phone-settings/after-save-390.png">after save</a> show the interaction, not a fix. The owning repair remains for human review; invalid-save phone continuation is not qualified.</li><li>Search snippets select the title column even for body-text matches. Matching field notes now use a short published opening-paragraph preview when the snippet is absent or redundant; useful native snippets and result ranking stay unchanged. This is a discovery sharp edge with a merchant fallback, not a CMS patch or an upstream report.</li></ul></section><section id="costs"><h2>Activity & costs</h2>
    <p>Recorded metadata refreshes with telemetry, independently of agent cycles. Controller results and retained conversation records have different scopes: a missing final response is not evidence that a cycle failed.</p>
    <dl class="status-list" data-activity-metrics>
      <div><dt>Controller-reported successful runs</dt><dd data-successful-runs>{numeric(activity?.controller?.successfulRuns)}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Last controller result</dt><dd>{show(activity?.controller?.lastResult)} · {show(activity?.controller?.lastCompletedAt)}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Retained cycle prompts</dt><dd>{numeric(activity?.cyclePrompts)}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Prompts with a final response</dt><dd>{numeric(activity?.cyclesWithFinalResponse)}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Average prompt-to-final window</dt><dd>{minutes(activity?.averagePromptToFinalSeconds)}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Retained sessions / compactions</dt><dd>{numeric(activity?.sessions)} / {numeric(activity?.compactions)}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Latest recorded model</dt><dd>{show(activity?.latestModel?.model)} · {show(activity?.latestModel?.provider)}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Latest reasoning level</dt><dd>{show(activity?.latestModel?.reasoning)}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Recorded model time</dt><dd>{minutes(activity?.recordedModelSeconds)}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Input tokens · uncached</dt><dd>{numeric(activity?.tokens?.input)}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Output tokens</dt><dd>{numeric(activity?.tokens?.output)}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Cached tokens · read / written</dt><dd>{numeric(activity?.tokens?.cacheRead)} / {numeric(activity?.tokens?.cacheWrite)}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Reasoning tokens · included in output</dt><dd>{numeric(activity?.tokens?.reasoning)}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Total tokens processed</dt><dd data-recorded-tokens>{numeric(activity?.tokens?.totalTokens)}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Usage records</dt><dd>{numeric(activity?.usageRecords)} · {activity ? activity.usageComplete ? 'available usage fields complete in parsed records' : 'partial coverage' : 'Unavailable'}</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <p>Token counts cover assistant and compaction requests, including repeated cached context—not unique words. Prompt-to-final windows exclude cycles without a retained final response and are not full process runtimes. Rotation, commit and deployment totals are not yet collected.</p>
    <dl class="status-list">
      <div><dt>Recorded API-equivalent estimate</dt><dd data-api-equivalent>{dollars(activity?.apiEquivalentUSD)} · {activity ? activity.costComplete ? 'recorded request costs complete' : 'partial cost coverage' : 'Unavailable'}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Actual billed cost to date</dt><dd>Unavailable · request estimates and budget rates are not an invoice</dd></div>
      <div><dt>LLM subscription budget</dt><dd>$100 / month</dd></div><div><dt>Server budget</dt><dd>$12 / month</dd></div><div><dt>Domain registration budget</dt><dd>$20 / year</dd></div>
    </dl>
